WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.560
Reports of a nuclear satellite launch within 60 days push NATO to vow space defense. This is Omni View Top World News, Episode 63. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. After that, a meningitis warning in Gaza, and video's chief back in the job, and how index funds tie savers to the AI trade. German public broadcasters and a newspaper in an account carried by the BBC say anonymous military and intelligence sources described a satellite called Sputnik-S.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:34.020
Fitted with a nuclear warhead and able to disrupt or destroy other satellites.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:40.660
France 24 adds that those accounts cite the BND as well as the military, and speak of a launch in the coming weeks.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.800
It is not clear which country wrote the intelligence that Ally shared this month.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:48.400
Chancellor Friedrich Murs neither confirmed nor denied the reports.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:54.100
He called them not new and still shocking, and said they show how far Russia is prepared to escalate.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:58.340
While spokesman Stefan Cornelius said Berlin is taking them very seriously,

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:01.520
and also warned against panic over hypothetical dangers.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.400
Dimitri Peskov said he had not seen the reports

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.540
and that stories built on unknown sources

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.280
are hardly worth taking seriously.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:10.840
The Russian Embassy in Berlin called the claims

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.860
unfounded and a propaganda campaign.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.980
Mark Ruda, standing with MERS, said the alliance

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:18.560
has a range of responses and will update deterrence

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:19.000
where it must.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:22.520
Russia has signed the 1967 outer space treaty,

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.260
which bars weapons of mass destruction from orbit.

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:31.240
Joseph Ashbacher of the European Space Agency called Nuclear Weapons in Space the Ultimate Nightmare,

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:36.280
and Blood &amp; Bowen told the BBC a blast would hit more than 15,000 active satellites,

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:39.460
and would be indiscriminate enough to wreck Russian craft 2.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:45.300
In 2024, the United States accused Russia of developing a nuclear-armed anti-satellite weapon.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:51.240
Russia denied it, and Vladimir Putin said Moscow was still categorically against nuclear weapons in space.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:57.240
Gaza health officials told Al Jazeera at least seven Palestinians were killed in Israeli strikes,

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:02.260
among them a child and police officers, as the health ministry put out an epidemic alert for

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:08.880
meningitis. Dr. Nadal Gohnaim said October brought 272 cases, more than eight times a normal

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:13.660
month of 30 to 50, and that 15 people have died of the disease since the start of this year.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.920
Five of those deaths in August, September, and October.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:22.460
However, bacterial meningitis, the dangerous form, hit 108 cases in October against a

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:26.900
usual 10-20, and another 100 cases have been logged since November began.

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:29.280
The ministry says thousands are at risk.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:33.600
Children most of all, because health and environmental conditions have deteriorated.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.560
Medical sources said three people, including a child, died in a strike on Wadi Gaza.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:44.540
Wafa said an Israeli drone strike on Al-Mawasi, west of Kahn Unis, killed three and wounded

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:45.000
five.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.280
Hind Kudari reported those three were police officers.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:53.660
Wafa also said one person died of injuries after being targeted in Jabalia, and that two

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:55.940
civilians were killed Monday night in Gaza City.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:01.080
Kudari said dozens more were hurt, and that strikes have gone on daily, even though a cease-fire

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:01.620
was agreed.

00:03:02.722 --> 00:03:07.662
Jensen Huang is back as Nvidia's chief executive, less than two weeks after a forced resignation

00:03:07.662 --> 00:03:12.342
over extra marital affairs, including one with a woman suspected of spying for China.

00:03:12.342 --> 00:03:16.662
And the BBC reports the board reversed itself after Donald Trump pressed it.

00:03:17.002 --> 00:03:18.222
Trump said he made the deal.

00:03:18.622 --> 00:03:23.122
He told CNBC the board wanted assurance on the national security threat and got assurance

00:03:23.122 --> 00:03:24.882
is based on everything officials know.

00:03:25.362 --> 00:03:29.842
He called losing Huang the real threat, and when asked if the stock drop after the resignation

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:32.202
shaped his choice, he said probably so.

00:03:32.842 --> 00:03:34.462
Huang resigned on the 12th of November.

00:03:35.042 --> 00:03:37.422
Last Tuesday, the board said it would not bring him back.

00:03:37.422 --> 00:03:42.362
Chairman Harvey Jones then said the return served stockholders, employees, partners and

00:03:42.362 --> 00:03:46.662
customers, and that senior U.S. government input left the board confident there was no

00:03:46.662 --> 00:03:47.982
national security risk.

00:03:48.422 --> 00:03:53.662
The BBC says the comeback added almost $1 trillion to Nvidia's market value, as the share

00:03:53.662 --> 00:03:58.522
price jumped 31 percent, pulling other tech shares and Asian markets up, while European

00:03:58.522 --> 00:03:59.662
markets stayed flat.

00:04:00.122 --> 00:04:04.142
The price is still down over the past month on wider worries about the AI industry.

00:04:04.142 --> 00:04:09.522
Longmakers are angry, and Huang is due before Congress next week over his ties to Alice

00:04:09.522 --> 00:04:11.702
Huang, alleged to be a Chinese spy.

00:04:12.262 --> 00:04:13.122
China denies that.

00:04:13.622 --> 00:04:17.202
On Monday, the Commerce Department said it was preparing to blacklist mega-speed.

00:04:17.622 --> 00:04:21.802
The Singapore customer where Alice Huang, no relation, was chief executive.

00:04:22.322 --> 00:04:27.542
A BBC review of disclosures found Trump bought Nvidia shares worth between $23 and $86

00:04:27.542 --> 00:04:34.122
million over two years, including a $265,000 purchase and sales of as much as $15,000

00:04:34.122 --> 00:04:40.822
dollars in September, across 85 purchases. Huang is 63 and co-founded the company in 1993.

00:04:42.051 --> 00:04:47.891
The MSCI All-Country World Index, DW reports, is nearly two-thirds invested in U.S.

00:04:48.171 --> 00:04:51.671
listed companies, even though those firms are only about a fifth of the list.

00:04:52.171 --> 00:04:57.931
Gurd Commer, a German asset manager, told DW a portfolio that is 70% in one country

00:04:57.931 --> 00:05:02.811
does not represent the global economy, which he said is tougher than any single national economy.

00:05:02.811 --> 00:05:07.231
He wants every sector in the mix, and no sector above a quarter of a portfolio.

00:05:07.791 --> 00:05:12.351
These flagship funds buy by market value, so a company that grows larger automatically

00:05:12.351 --> 00:05:16.851
takes a bigger share, and they hold pensions and savings for hundreds of millions of passive

00:05:16.851 --> 00:05:17.331
investors.

00:05:17.911 --> 00:05:21.351
Nine of that global indexes top 10 names are US big tech.

00:05:21.891 --> 00:05:26.491
The 10th is TSMC, which makes 90% of high-end AI semiconductors.

00:05:26.911 --> 00:05:29.251
Those 10 names are nearly a quarter of the index.

00:05:29.251 --> 00:05:34.351
In the emerging market index, the top 10 are 37.5% of value.

00:05:34.811 --> 00:05:40.711
TSMC alone almost 16% and eight of the largest holdings are tech, chip, or internet firms,

00:05:40.991 --> 00:05:43.451
beside one Chinese bank and one Indian bank.

00:05:43.951 --> 00:05:49.151
Dimitri Veyanos of the London School of Economics told DW his model finds index fund flows

00:05:49.151 --> 00:05:54.571
push prices harder when the biggest stocks sit in the same industry because funds keep adding to winners.

00:05:54.571 --> 00:06:00.271
economists told DW that as partly why investors hunting shelter from the AI trade are finding

00:06:00.271 --> 00:06:01.271
few places left.

00:06:02.446 --> 00:06:06.306
Canada is where a Quebec court has put the Royal Oath back in front of the legislature.

00:06:06.926 --> 00:06:11.046
The Globe and Mail reports Justice Ian Demers ruled that provincial members must swear

00:06:11.046 --> 00:06:15.206
allegiance to King Charles III before they can take their seats in the National Assembly.

00:06:15.746 --> 00:06:21.046
He suspended, on an emergency application, a 2022 law that had scrapped fealty to the

00:06:21.046 --> 00:06:21.626
British monarch.

00:06:21.626 --> 00:06:26.786
He wrote that the oath, contrary to how it may look, plays a vital role in democracy,

00:06:27.106 --> 00:06:31.226
because it acknowledges the primacy of the Constitution, personified by the king.

00:06:31.846 --> 00:06:37.306
After the October 5 election, all 127 legislators swore only to the people of Quebec.

00:06:37.886 --> 00:06:39.886
The National Assembly is due back next week.

00:06:40.366 --> 00:06:41.846
The decision was released Tuesday.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:48.160
Elsewhere, Malaysia is set to send thousands of Rohingya refugees back to Myanmar, Al Jazeera

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:52.580
reports. Five days after the International Court of Justice ruled that Myanmar committed

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:57.200
genocide against that minority. The Wall Street Journal reports the European Union has

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:01.000
inked a trade deal with Indonesia to cut tariffs and catalyze investment.

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:06.880
France 24 reports Pakistan's Muhammad Zishan Ali is due Wednesday as the first foreign

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:12.040
astronaut on China's Tian Gong station, and he says he will carry the hopes of 250 million

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:17.960
Pakistanis. The New York Times reports Japan's leader, Senya Takaiqi, welcomed the International

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:22.620
Criminal Court's president and vowed to speed financial support even as the Trump administration

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:23.840
tries to cripple the court.

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:29.440
CBC reports Britain's Labour Prime Minister, Andy Burnham, has nudged open the door to

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:33.600
closer European Union ties, a shift some are already calling a brief turn.

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:36.140
That's OmniView top-world news for today.

